to fall to pieces or to dust, decay, be ruined, perish, RV. &c. &c.;
to be gone, vanish (only Impv. ध्वंस, ˚सत, ˚सताम्), MBh.; Hariv.; R.;
to scatter, cover &c. (only ध्वस्त, q.v.) :
Pass. ध्वस्यते (Pāṇ. vi, 4, 24, Kāś.);
 ˚ति (GopBr.) to be destroyed, perish:
Caus. ध्वंस॑यति, ˚ते, to scatter, TBr.;
to destroy, disperse, disturb, R.; Daś.;
to violate (a woman), Kathās.;
 ध्वस॑यति, to scintillate, sparkle (Agni), RV. i, 140, 3; 5 :
